<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadri Maqsudi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1957</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sadreddin Maksudi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadri Maqsudi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> lawyer and politician who sat in the Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-duma">State Duma</a> and led efforts for Muslim autonomy after the 1917 revolution. He was a leader of the project for an Idel-Ural State in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> region. After the Bolsheviks suppressed it he emigrated, and he later taught law in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> and became a Turkish member of parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sadri-maqsudi.jpg" alt="Sadri Maqsudi" width="180" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sadri_Maksudi_Bey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
